  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-27T12:31:19.251Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since only the creator can ban a malicious user from their world, it is crucial that the world creator cannot be blocked from \"banning\" a user in their world (currently just a 1-hour kick that will hopefully be extended to something more useful in the future). \nUnfortunately, this is currently easily possible to evade, since the user disappears in all social lists they block you, which seems to be an oversight from VRChat since this gives malicious users a really easy way to bypass any ban. \nFurthermore, being blocked at all in your own world from someone shouldn't be possible at all IMHO to avoid evading world bans.\nTo give you an example, I just politely told someone that I would appreciate it if they don't use an NSFW avatar in public instances of our world and just got blocked as a result, being unable to kick this person from the world. I don't think kicking without politely asking the person first would be a good solution, but it seems that this is the only way. However, a malicious user can currently just block the world creators first to make them unable to even see their misbehaving in the first place - clearly a system that should be changed.",
